{"author":"Blake Wayne Allcorn","body":"codex/chapters/01-aethel-4b-story-v3.md","body_bytes":46623,"body_sha256":"de72f3c9c687741235c3f2db006fffae3735538405bcfa96574592f1dff12902","date":"2026-11-24","id":"chapter.01","kind":"chapter","note":"Plane A anchor. The storyteller continues from this chapter's final beat.","plane":"A","renders":["render.01","render.02","render.03","render.04","render.05"],"status":"active-chronicle","title":"Aethel 4-B (Story v3)"}
{"author":"Blake Wayne Allcorn","body":"codex/chapters/02-the-chord-of-eight-weights.md","body_bytes":9533,"body_sha256":"783690bd395de3498a100f8b0311cdeaefd9d2593aaa3aceb3b93d95bae983c4","id":"chapter.02","kind":"chapter","note":"From the Aethel-4B world file. Covers the same Vault Four / Leviathan / chord beats as Story v3 in a telemetry-dense register. Kept verbatim for reference; not used as the continuity anchor. See the Provenance page.","plane":"A","source":{"document":"Aethel-4B","lines":[593,659]},"status":"parallel-draft","title":"Chapter II: The Chord of Eight Weights"}
{"aliases":["Alkor-Seven","polar envoy","polar weaver"],"canon":["Mirror-polished bismuth plates that shimmer aurora-violet; he glides a fraction lighter over magnetized iron-stone.","Six whip-antennae crown his skull and crackle with pale plasma halos; they taste the electromagnetic wind.","His chest coils drink the dark star's magnetic pull and release it as a magnetic pinch that locks offworld metal and ferro-fluid joints.","Heat is death to his kind: if his core runs a few degrees too hot, the coils in his chest burn out."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":126},"gear":[],"id":"character.alkor-seven","kind":"character","lineage":"race.auror-sith","plane":"B","pronoun":"he","role":"Auror-Sith envoy from the freezing polar calderas","source_lines":[126,140,182,211,285,296],"tells":["tilted his mirrored head while his antennae stiffened, tasting the air","planted all six limbs on the iron-stone before he let a charge go"],"title":"Alkor-Seven","voice":"crisp, unhurried, quiet; frost at the edges of his words"}
{"aliases":["Baryon-Nine","the deep-dweller","deep-walker","the ancient"],"canon":["Squat, six-legged and centaurian, plated in black diamond-hard ceramic; two rotary diamond fore-augers.","Its mind stays sharp only while fire glows under its belly and frost hisses off its back-fins; cold surface stone locks its thoughts.","It speaks in a rumble felt through shin-bones and boot soles rather than ears.","Its augers can drum a herding heartbeat through bedrock and turn stone to mire."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":136},"gear":["rotary diamond fore-augers","dorsal lug behind its radiator fins (Kael-Thon's tow point)"],"id":"character.baryon-nine","kind":"character","lineage":"race.osmir-dreg","plane":"B","pronoun":"it","role":"Osmir-Dreg ancient who surfaced when the invaders pierced its brood-fault","source_lines":[136,138,178,180,223,225,311,313],"tells":["lowered its armored prow and read the deep stone through its hooves","let a slow rumble roll up through the ground before it spoke"],"title":"Baryon-Nine","voice":"slow, monumental, speaks of 'our brood-fault' and 'the hound'"}
{"aliases":["Brek-Gron","Lock-Warden"],"canon":["Eyeless and plated in pitted black magnetite; the electromagnetic pits along his cheeks drink in charge from the air.","Dark ferro-lubricant weeps from his pressurized shoulder seams under the night weight and steams in the cold.","He reads speech through stone and answers with thumps of his underslung mandibular ram.","Disciplined in the deep-vault way, until he sees his people's iron stitched with offworld silver."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":93},"gear":["three-clawed hydraulic gauntlet","hydraulic accumulators in his hips"],"id":"character.brek-gron","kind":"character","lineage":"race.khor-gron","plane":"B","pronoun":"he","role":"Lock-Warden of the vault beneath Vault Four's airlock rim","source_lines":[93,98,100,112,187,233,300,301],"tells":["struck his mandibular ram once against the stone before he spoke","tapped his jaw-horn against his own chest plate","thumped a soft two-beat recognition against the stone"],"title":"Brek-Gron","voice":"few words, low and grinding; calls Sera-Vash 'half-stone'"}
{"aliases":["Chorus-Root-04","the Cantor","Cantor"],"canon":["Stitched together from the donated shells of dead flyers and vault-guards; its chest lattice pulses with emerald-gold light threads.","Two amber resonance bells: the left booms a deep nocturnal bass into a Khor-Gron jaw, the longer right whistles a clear noon-tone.","It speaks as We-of-Spire-Seven and can read a severed control-leash by pressing glowing tendrils to it.","It vents fogs of golden silica spores and roots its heel-tendrils into living root-bark to sing through the spire."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":126},"gear":[],"id":"character.chorus-root-04","kind":"character","lineage":"race.myco-choir","plane":"B","pronoun":"it","role":"Ambulatory Myco-Choir Cantor that speaks for We-of-Spire-Seven","source_lines":[126,129,146,207,292,307,308],"tells":["sank its glowing heel-tendrils into the nearest root or stone","turned its amber bells toward the one it meant to speak to"],"title":"Chorus-Root-04","voice":"dual-voiced, plural ('We-of-Spire-Seven'), calm and urgent at once"}
{"aliases":["the kneeling Iron-Blood","Vault Twelve"],"canon":["Taken three seasons back when Vault Twelve's eastern airlock cracked; his clan mark still shows beneath the tungsten sutures.","A single red eye grafted above his jaw; his voice is a rusted, metallic scrape.","He knows the Spike's main ballast locks lie up the flooded intake tunnel, and that the flyer's lungs will not survive the sulfur gas inside."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":296},"gear":["cracked silver Kolvax control-collar"],"id":"character.iron-blood-vault-twelve","kind":"character","lineage":"hybrid.iron-bloods","plane":"B","pronoun":"he","role":"Former Khor-Gron of Vault Twelve, rebuilt in the Kolvax vats; freed of his control-collar","source_lines":[296,300,301,303,316,318],"tells":["struck his fist once against his own chest plate"],"title":"Iron-Blood of Vault Twelve (unnamed)","voice":"rasping, hates the iron-men who rebuilt him"}
{"aliases":["Kael-Thon","the nomad","wind-skater"],"canon":["Low, wedge-headed, with a copper-green airfoil carapace and a fluted venturi along his spine that howls a twilight note.","He breathes by ram-air: without a fast wind forcing air through his back-flutes he begins to drown in still air.","Braided harpoon cables with carbide pitons anchor him; wind-gathered static discharges violet down the wire."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":121},"gear":["four carbide skates","braided harpoon cables with carbide pitons","wrist-line"],"id":"character.kael-thon","kind":"character","lineage":"race.zephyr-krel","plane":"B","pronoun":"he","role":"Zephyr-Krel nomad who tacks the Grinding Gale on carbide skates","source_lines":[121,152,176,196,198,276,278],"tells":["leaned hard against his taut harpoon wire so the air screamed through his back-flutes","grounded his sparking skates against dry rock"],"title":"Kael-Thon","voice":"wastes no breath; acts before he answers"}
{"aliases":["Sera-Vash","Sera","half-stone","Vesper"],"canon":["A Vesper, born of the twilight buffer canyons where the sky-clans and the vault-clans met; neither stratum lets her forget it.","Her mother's people are the pearl-skinned canopy flyers; she wears gunmetal-slate skin and short braking vanes instead.","By day her ferro-marrow sloshes loose and light enough to drop through the sun-shafts; at dusk it stiffens like cold mercury until her footfalls ring.","She speaks through a dual-throated syrinx: a high fluted register for the noon wind, a lower gravelly chamber that a Khor-Gron jaw can read.","Opening both throats at once hurts like swallowing crushed glass, but it makes her the bridge between the noon and the nadir."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":56},"gear":["brass balance-beam","iron-weighted bone pike","chest-harness packed with dried spore-resin"],"id":"character.sera-vash","kind":"character","lineage":"hybrid.vespers","plane":"B","pronoun":"she","role":"Vesper tariff-collector on the lowest external tariff-shelf of Spire-Seven","source_lines":[56,58,60,62,63,96,189,194],"tells":["unhooked her brass balance-beam and weighed the goods before she named a toll","tapped the counter-weight with a slate-gray claw","dropped a hand to the iron-weighted bone pike at her hip","planted the pike-butt in the dirt to keep her footing"],"title":"Sera-Vash","voice":"clipped, practical, a trader's bluntness; calls Brek-Gron 'Lock-Warden'"}
{"aliases":["Vora-Nai","river-warden","sluice-warden"],"canon":["Cobalt-and-teal mantle, six crimson gill-frills that purge pressurized brine, a long golden-studded tail-keel.","Her tail-line hears vibrations through water and pipe; the golden studs flare teal when she listens.","She spits a needle-thin lance of brine and stone-slurry that can score offworld metal.","In flooded water she is in her true element; she moves like a dark eel through murk."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel_4-B_Story(v3)","line":82},"gear":[],"id":"character.vora-nai","kind":"character","lineage":"race.siphon-naiad","plane":"B","pronoun":"she","role":"Siphon-Naiad sluice-warden of Sinkhole Four's draining whirlpool","source_lines":[82,123,158,231,243,245,282],"tells":["raised a webbed, four-clawed hand in brief acknowledgment","flattened her body against the submerged metal to listen with her tail"],"title":"Vora-Nai","voice":"hissed, urgent, precise about what the water tells her"}
{"aliases":["Zhur-09","Centurion Zhur-09"],"canon":["Sintered tungsten plates, a jawless tri-visor helmet, and twin rings of spinning mercury caged between his shoulder blades.","Sera-Vash drove her pike between his cervical steam-ports; he lies still, mercury leaking from a fractured valve."],"first_appearance":{"document":"Aethel-4B (Chapter II)","line":599},"gear":["flechette carbine"],"id":"character.zhur-09","kind":"character","lineage":"race.kolvax","plane":"B","pronoun":"he","role":"Kolvax Centurion knocked unconscious at the rim of Vault Four (named only in Chapter II)","source_lines":[599,603],"status":"unconscious at the rim of Vault Four","tells":[],"title":"Zhur-09","voice":""}
{"anchor_chapter":"chapter.01","anchor_line":318,"id":"chronicle.seed","kind":"chronicle-seed","plane":"A","state":{"clock":{"label":"the sinking shaft reaches the liquid core-tide","minutes_remaining":12},"cycle_phi":0.3,"fatigue":{"character.alkor-seven":"severe","character.baryon-nine":"restored while its belly stays on the hot pipe","character.brek-gron":"moderate","character.chorus-root-04":"light","character.kael-thon":"severe: cannot breathe in still air without a tow","character.sera-vash":"heavy","character.vora-nai":"light: in her element"},"gear":{"character.baryon-nine":["rotary diamond fore-augers"],"character.brek-gron":["three-clawed hydraulic gauntlet"],"character.kael-thon":["one harpoon line still tethered to Baryon-Nine","one harpoon spent in an Iron-Blood's optic"],"character.sera-vash":["iron-weighted bone pike","brass balance-beam","chest-harness"]},"injuries":{"character.alkor-seven":["overheated coils from the steam; close to burning out"],"character.brek-gron":["cracked seam beneath the collarbone, leaking oil","stiff shoulder oil after the magnetic lock"],"character.iron-blood-vault-twelve":["jaw-horn broken; speaks only in a rasp"],"character.sera-vash":["nosebleed from the Leviathan's roar","scalded from the trench slush"]},"last_line":"\"The main ballast locks are thirty paces up the intake tunnel, Lock-Warden,\" the hybrid rasped, his single red eye gleaming in the dark steam as he nodded toward the flooded black mouth of the pipe. \"Your drills can't break the pins alone—and the flyer's lungs won't survive the sulfur gas inside. Who swims the pipe with me?\"","location":"location.spike-cooling-trench","offstage":["fauna.nadir-leviathan","character.zhur-09"],"positions":{"character.baryon-nine":"straddling the hot cooling pipe","character.chorus-root-04":"kneeling in the shallow wash","character.iron-blood-vault-twelve":"standing in the mud, gripping Brek-Gron's wrist","character.sera-vash":"one boot on the rim of the burst pipe"},"pov":"character.sera-vash","present":["character.sera-vash","character.brek-gron","character.vora-nai","character.kael-thon","character.alkor-seven","character.chorus-root-04","character.baryon-nine","character.iron-blood-vault-twelve"],"promises":[{"by":"character.sera-vash","text":"We don't split, and we don't climb: the company stays together on the low road."},{"by":"character.baryon-nine","text":"The hound rising from the brood-fault is ours; clear it a path to the eastern spire."}],"tension":[{"id":"ballast-drop","text":"Their Primarch ordered an emergency drop: mercury ballast is venting from the upper towers so the mile-high Spike sinks under its own weight into the magma fault before dawn. The drill-head far below has unlocked its brakes; when the shaft hits the liquid core-tide, the back-splash will boil every aquifer and vault for leagues.","weight":5},{"id":"who-swims","text":"The freed Iron-Blood asked who will swim the flooded intake tunnel with him to the ballast locks; the flyer's lungs cannot survive the sulfur gas.","weight":5},{"id":"vats","text":"The Leviathan has breached the citadel's central foundry floor ahead; the invaders are abandoning the lower cloning vats, and no more soldiers are coming from this conduit.","weight":3},{"id":"null-gyros","text":"The Null-Gyro flock wheeled back in confusion when the tower's beacon stuttered; it will not stay confused.","weight":2},{"id":"alkor-heat","text":"Alkor-Seven's coils are close to burning out in the steam.","weight":2},{"id":"kael-breath","text":"Kael-Thon can only breathe while something tows him fast enough.","weight":2}]},"title":"Seed: the flooded cooling trench beneath the Baryon-Spike"}
{"finding_id":"story.two-drafts-of-one-beat","id":"conflict.narrative-01","kind":"conflict","method":"Story v3 is used as the Plane A anchor for the chronicle; Chapter II is kept in the reader marked as a parallel draft and is never fed to the voice.","plane":"D","severity":"parallel-draft","source":"Story v3 paragraphs 1-320; Aethel-4B lines 593-659","subjects":["chapter.02"],"title":"Two tellings of the same beats: Story v3 and the Chapter II text (The Chord of Eight Weights) both narrate the Vault Four ambush, the Leviathan, the eight-voice chord and the core-tide descent with different wording and detail."}
